          "question": "What should I use instead for the knees?",
          "answer": "Before I suggest anything, could you tell me two things?\n\n1. **What do you currently use for your knees?** For example, ibuprofen, another pain reliever, a brace, a supplement, or nothing.\n2. **What would you like to replace it for?** For example, pain relief, a brace, exercise, or a medication.\n\nThe right choice depends on what is causing the knee problem. Only a clinician who examines your knees can work that out.\n\n**General options described in my sources:**\n\n- **Exercise is the core treatment.** For knee osteoarthritis, the guidance combines muscle strengthening around the knee, keeping the joint moving through its full range, and aerobic activity. The guidance says these are combined, not chosen between. It also says that starting with a supervised program helps, because the right movements and gradual progression are hard to judge alone. (Source: lifestyle-osteoarthritis-activity; guideline-osteoarthritis-management)\n- **Weight management where relevant.** The osteoarthritis overview lists body weight as a contributor and as part of treatment. (Source: condition-osteoarthritis)\n- **Topical anti-inflammatory gels.** The osteoarthritis guidance describes topical anti-inflammatory drugs as the preferred first medicine option for knee osteoarthritis, with lower whole-body exposure than tablets. Ask a clinician or pharmacist whether this suits you. (Source: guideline-osteoarthritis-management)\n- **Glucosamine and chondroitin are not recommended** by most bodies, because evidence shows no clinically meaningful effect. (Source: guideline-osteoarthritis-management)\n\nMy sources do not cover braces, specific exercises, or how to choose between options for your knees. Doses are outside what I can give.\n\n**Discuss with your clinician:** Your reflux and ibuprofen use matter when choosing any pain option, so mention both. Do not stop or change ibuprofen on your own.\n\n**Seek urgent care** for sudden severe knee pain with a hot, swollen knee and fever, or if you cannot bear weight, or if you have any of the bleeding or chest symptoms listed earlier.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational tool and must not be used for real medical decisions.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
